.TH DLEAPP 1 "2026" "DLEAPP" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dleapp \- Desktop Logs Events And Protobuf Parser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dleapp
[\-t \fItype\fR] [\-i \fIinput\fR] [\-o \fIoutput\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B dleapp
(no arguments opens the window)
.SH DESCRIPTION
DLEAPP parses artifacts left behind by desktop applications: the logs,
events, and stored data of Electron/Chromium-based desktop apps
(IndexedDB/LevelDB stores including protobuf-encoded values, Local Storage,
service-worker and HTTP caches, cookies, and application logs).
It is a member of the LEAPP family, built on the RLEAPP framework.
.PP
Started without arguments it opens the graphical window.
Given arguments in a terminal it runs as a command line tool.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-input " " \fItype\fR
Input type: \fBfs\fR (folder), \fBtar\fR, \fBzip\fR, \fBgz\fR, \fBraw\fR (disk image).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input_path " " \fIpath\fR
Path to the input file or folder.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output_path " " \fIpath\fR
Path to the base output folder (must already exist).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-load_profile " " \fIfile\fR
Path to a DLEAPP Profile file (.dlprofile).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the full help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/dleapp
Program files.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/dleapp
Symlink to the program.
